WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:04.970 --> 00:05.860
The main question is…

2
00:06.500 --> 00:11.870
What factors contribute to the go/no-go decision?
I was going with colour, size…

3
00:12.680 --> 00:15.390
It's hard to know. There's so much to consider.

4
00:17.890 --> 00:21.400
In this case, let's see if we can leverage our experience.

5
00:21.400 --> 00:25.400
Okay, yes, of course.
Perhaps similar projects could tell us something.

6
00:25.400 --> 00:29.400
Okay — what about last year? The floss project, right?

7
00:29.400 --> 00:35.480
Same thing. We were trying to decide
whether to enter the market with a new product.

8
00:35.560 --> 00:38.600
What was the critical data on that project?

9
00:38.600 --> 00:44.400
I remember hinging the decision
on what our customers were willing to pay for it.

10
00:44.400 --> 00:49.560
So the price point, right? But is it applicable here?

11
00:49.700 --> 00:53.400
The competitive landscape for both products is similar.

12
00:53.400 --> 00:56.600
Why didn't we think of this before?
— Well, we've thought of it now.

13
00:56.600 --> 01:00.800
And I'm thinking the price points are similar, and the target market.

14
01:00.800 --> 01:04.190
That is a great comparison across multiple dimensions. Nice work.

15
01:04.190 --> 01:08.200
Price — not colour or size.

16
01:08.200 --> 01:12.200
For now, yes. We'll just focus on the important questions.

17
01:12.200 --> 01:17.200
What are they willing to pay for this product?
That will be the focus of our research.

18
01:17.200 --> 01:20.960
I'm almost thinking now of the…
— The brightening strip project.

19
01:21.030 --> 01:27.970
Yes, so similar. And if I recall correctly,
a big piece of the critical data was… anyone?

20
01:30.120 --> 01:34.200
Performance specifications.
— Performance specifications.

21
01:34.200 --> 01:38.590
It was before you joined the company.
— Brightening strips, yeah, that's it.

22
01:38.950 --> 01:43.400
A good example. Anyway, what we found out
was that the decision came down to

23
01:43.400 --> 01:49.400
what performance specifications had to be equal to
or better than the competitors' products.

24
01:49.400 --> 01:55.320
So do they make your teeth whiter — or at least as white?
— Yeah.

25
01:55.400 --> 01:58.400
That was one of the most important ones, in fact.

26
01:58.400 --> 02:02.560
Let's quickly revise our research budget, assuming
that we're just focusing on these important questions.

27
02:14.090 --> 02:20.200
See — now we've come down from a 50-lakh proposed budget
to, I guess, 15 lakhs.

28
02:20.200 --> 02:21.800
That's awesome.

29
02:21.800 --> 02:28.120
Yeah — by tightly focusing our research on the questions
which have been helpful on similar projects in the past.

30
02:28.450 --> 02:31.400
What do you think? Are we ready to present?
— Yes.

31
02:31.400 --> 02:35.400
Let's go! Let's not keep Apoorva waiting. Let's go.

32
02:35.400 --> 02:39.840
Don't worry — colour and packaging, we'll get you next time.

33
02:50.570 --> 02:56.600
I think Apoorva was really impressed
by the clarity and focus of the proposal.

34
02:56.600 --> 02:58.600
And the price tag.

35
02:58.600 --> 03:01.670
Great job, guys. I'm very excited to find out
what our research tells us.
